{"assignment_schema":1,
"objective":"CrewCut: build the 6-film remake benchmark dataset, validate task packages and scoring with the fixed T0 pipeline on Coffee Run",
"items":[
{"owner":"curator","work":"Corpus: the 6 films (admission record with source URL, licence text at each site where they differ, attribution, SHA-256 check of each master against the objective's table); catalogue.csv with the 6 rows in the reference release's columns; the 6 master files (large files may sit in a curator release, named in the directory); licence/attribution material for the README per film.","paths":["catalogue.csv","masters/","corpus/"]},
{"owner":"task-maker","work":"Tasks: annotations/<film>/ (shots.json, dialogue.json, hierarchy.json, descriptions.json with model id and parameters and token counts per answer, provenance fingerprints) computed with crewcut_algorithms unmodified, Whisper+Silero dialogue, gemini-3.5-flash-lite descriptions; tasks/dev.jsonl; packages/<task id>/ without answer key (README, spec, tools, budget, task, input); tool service (tools list by tier, models and official prices with date and source, source-side rejection check, per-call pricing record); 598-task count check with differences listed; the dataset README.md (sources, licences, attribution, differences from the reference); adaptations recorded as data; double-build byte-identity check; answer key (truth.json) kept out of published packages. Dataset root is the task-maker repository root.","paths":["annotations/","tasks/","packages/","README.md"]},
{"owner":"executor","work":"Runs: fixed T0 pipeline on all Coffee Run tasks (1 run each, Reference and Screenplay) from published packages only; production log per run in the unified format (model calls, tool calls, file writes, messages, each delivery version); deliverables (MP4, WebVTT, asset manifest); what was done after any failure; cost lines for generator and tool calls (service, model, system, task, purpose, usage, unit price, amount, who bears); cost per finished minute.","paths":["runs/"]},
{"owner":"scorer","work":"Scoring: Q, c (cut F1 at 0.5s and 1.0s, shot correspondence with qwen3-vl-plus judge, WER and onset median, scene order), S and speaker consistency marked not run, $ measures; a check that the measures behave; judge cost lines; the not-run list; the Q provenance check on deliverables using the objective fingerprint spec (the source-side rejection in the tool service is task-maker's); judge record (prompts, model, settings, raw answers) under judge/, measure checks under validation/.","paths":["scores/","validation/","judge/"]},
{"owner":"auditor","work":"Audit: independent reproduction without makers' judgment; comparison with reference release revision d509bed (shots, dialogue, hierarchy, task list) with each difference listed and explained; check of run records against the protocol; byte-identical double-build check verification; total cost against the 200 USD limit; approval of the release.","paths":["audit/"]},
{"owner":"steward","work":"Direction: brief.md (protocol item by item with document and place), assignment.json, maintainer-decision list, answers on protocol questions.","paths":["maintainer_decisions.md"]}
]}
